(Bug #64: `the` is only an article before a variable name
 (LANGUAGE.md:1857), so `the h's size` and `h's size` are the same
 reading. The `the` spelling knew none of the file properties and
 answered "Expected property name" for every one but `size`. Every row
 of the File Properties table, read through the `the` spelling.)

open a file for writing called setup at "/tmp/vox_test_the_file_props.txt".
Write "hello vox" to setup.
Close setup.

open a file for reading called reader at "/tmp/vox_test_the_file_props.txt".

Print "size: {the reader's size}".

If the reader's descriptor is greater than -1 then,
    Print "descriptor: open".

Print "readable: {the reader's readable}".
Print "writable: {the reader's writable}".

If the reader's modified is greater than 0 then,
    Print "modified: a timestamp".

If the reader's accessed is greater than 0 then,
    Print "accessed: a timestamp".

If the reader's permissions is greater than 0 then,
    Print "permissions: a mode".

Close reader.

open a file for writing called writer at "/tmp/vox_test_the_file_props.txt".
Print "writer readable: {the writer's readable}".
Print "writer writable: {the writer's writable}".
Close writer.

Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_the_file_props.txt".
